          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "A product can work beautifully…"
        },
        {
          "id": "text-complexity-listen",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 8.05,
          "focusWU": 8.45,
          "endWU": 8.85,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.8,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "…and still tell the wrong story."
        },
        {
          "id": "text-discipline-labels",
          "kind": "scroll-block",
          "startWU": 8.95,
          "focusWU": 9.7,
          "endWU": 11.4,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.6,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "reading-start"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "disciplines"
          },
          "block": {
            "id": "discipline-labels",
            "kind": "disciplines",
            "label": "Disciplines",
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "product-design",
                "label": "Product Design",
                "description": "I shape how something works, so a complex product feels clear from the first interaction."
              },
              {
                "id": "experience-design",
                "label": "Experience Design",
                "description": "I connect the moments around a product, so the experience makes sense as people move through it."
              },
              {
                "id": "art-direction",
                "label": "Art Direction",
                "description": "I give the work a visual point of view, because appearance is part of how it communicates."
              },
              {
                "id": "motion-and-3d",
                "label": "Motion & 3D",
                "description": "I use movement and space to explain change and make unfamiliar ideas easier to grasp."
              },
              {
                "id": "creative-engineering",
                "label": "Creative Engineering",
                "description": "I combine code and AI to turn early thinking into prototypes we can test."
              },
              {
                "id": "parametric-systems",
                "label": "Parametric Systems",
                "description": "I build systems that help the work scale without losing the details that give it character."
              }
            ]
          },
          "reveal": {
            "fadeDurationWU": 0.2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-disciplines-title",
          "kind": "scroll-block",
          "startWU": 11.5,
          "focusWU": 12.1,
          "endWU": 14.4,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.8,
            "gapAfter": "chapter",
            "focusMode": "reading-start"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "disciplines"
          },
          "block": {
            "id": "disciplines-passage",
            "kind": "stack",
            "modules": [
              {
                "id": "attention",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Products do not arrive in the world as wireframes. They arrive as things people see, read, feel, use and remember."
              },
              {
                "id": "brief-emphasis",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "The interesting part is how disciplines alter one another."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "friction-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Product design, visual communication, art direction, motion, systems and code all shape this relationship. Each offers a different way to understand the problem and make the answer feel coherent. When they begin influencing one another early, the work starts to feel like one thing rather than a collection of good decisions."
              },
              {
                "id": "trend-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I began in Communication Design, and the work gradually took me into products, experiences, visual identities, motion, 3D, systems and code. Over thirteen years, I’ve done that inside companies, in agencies, independently and as a consultant. The contexts have changed, but the pleasure has stayed the same: bringing different ways of thinking together around one thing."
              },
              {
                "id": "making-early",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Aesthetics matter to me because they do real work. They can give an unfamiliar service character, make new technology feel less alien and show people that someone has paid attention to the details."
              },
              {
                "id": "ai-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I use AI most days, usually alongside code, to explore directions, make prototypes and see how an idea behaves before it becomes expensive to change. It has opened up a remarkable amount of creative territory. It also has a habit of making everything look convincing."
              },
              {
                "id": "ambitious-teams",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "The questions I keep coming back to are simple: is it useful, does it have character, and is it responsible? AI can generate options, but it cannot decide which one should exist. That is still human work."
              },
              {
                "id": "unfinished-projects",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I’m at my best when there is no established answer yet, when a product, service or idea needs to become approachable without being made ordinary. I like getting close to the craft, staying with the question and giving it a form people can relate to. It is the work I love, and after thirteen years, I know I’m good at it."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-life-momentum",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 14.5,
          "focusWU": 14.85,
          "endWU": 15.2,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.7,
            "gapAfter": "tight",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "New ideas need a way in…"
        },
        {
          "id": "text-life-form",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 15.3,
          "focusWU": 15.65,
          "endWU": 16,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.7,
            "gapAfter": "tight",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "…and the right disciplines to shape them…"
        },
        {
          "id": "text-life-character",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 16.1,
          "focusWU": 16.45,
          "endWU": 16.8,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.7,
            "gapAfter": "chapter",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "…then something new becomes possible."
        },
        {
          "id": "text-epilogue-invitation",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 20.1,
          "focusWU": 20.65,
          "endWU": 22,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.4,
            "gapAfter": "none",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "text-finale-cta"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "finale-v1",
          "titleStyle": "display",
          "text": "Let’s begin.",
          "description": "If you’re working on something new, complex or still taking shape, I’d love to hear about it."
        }
      ]
    },
